Let $f(n)$ denote the sum of the numbers in the $n$th row.  We start by looking at an example.

Suppose we take the 5th row, make a copy of every number, and send each copy to the fifth row.

[asy]
unitsize (1 cm);

pair A, B;
int i;

for (i = 1; i <= 5; ++i) {
  A = (2*i - 1,1);
	B = (2*i - 2,0);
	draw(interp(A,B,0.2)--interp(A,B,0.7),Arrow(6));
	A = (2*i - 1,1);
	B = (2*i,0);
	draw(interp(A,B,0.2)--interp(A,B,0.7),Arrow(6));
}

